```

This combines both: huge window (no flip) + huge wait cap + abort → CANCELLED. With the overflow bug, the entry would expire at 1ms before the abort... actually abort happens synchronously right after acquire, before any timer — it'd be cancelled anyway. Hmm, to make it bite, await sleep(50) before abort: with the bug, entry already expired (expired=1, abort no-op); with fix, cancelled=1. Let me add the sleep.

